## Orbit rings are rasterized by [constant ORBITS_SHADER] from the camera matrices: every pixel
## measures its distance to each ring in screen pixels. A 3D ribbon foreshortens below one render
## pixel on the far side of each ellipse, and an antialiased polyline loses its corners there, so
## both break into dots at hairline widths; the analytic distance stays continuous.
const ORBIT_SAMPLES := 512
## The sampled polyline is slightly smaller than the true ellipse, and the stroke is drawn at the
## analytic curve, so the early-out box grows by a few pixels to avoid clipping the ring ends.
const ORBIT_BOUNDS_MARGIN_PX := 4.0
## Stroke width in screen pixels. Below one pixel the stroke keeps its center but dims, so it can
